{
 "_": "fs-mouth (11-11): the permanent teeth's default dimensions for one adult woman, as tunable defaults with their sources (design: varied data -> a tunable per-person target with a cited default). mm. Codes: U = maxillary, L = mandibular; 1 central incisor, 2 lateral, 3 canine, 4 first premolar, 5 second premolar, 6 first molar, 7 second molar. Keys: H anatomical crown length (labial CEJ to edge / buccal cusp tip), L root length, md / md_c mesiodistal width at the contacts / at the cervix, ll / ll_c labiolingual width at its height of contour / at the cervix, cej_m / cej_d the CEJ's rise on the mesial / distal face. Shape keys (cusps, ridges, roots, profile factors) are the form's own description, set by eye against the references (E). q: M measured in the cited source, D derived here (say how), E estimated (say why).",
 "sources": {
  "R1": "Rakhshan V et al. BioMed Res Int 2022;8381436 (331 casts, 257 F / 74 M, MD / BL, mean of sides; via engine/packs/human/research/mouth_teeth_tongue.md s.2)",
  "SAB13": "Saboia 2013 Brazilian women, casts: crown MD and BL (via the project's mouth research notes)",
  "R5": "Roca-Obis P et al. Acta Odontol Scand 2023;81:73-78: clinical crown heights, 83 women (caliper; worn teeth excluded)",
  "R7": "Basim A et al. Prog Orthod 2026;27:41: clinical crown heights incl. premolars and first molars at 31 y (mixed sex)",
  "WHEELER": "Wheeler's Dental Anatomy measurement table (cervical widths, root lengths, CEJ curvature), quoted from memory in mouth_teeth_tongue.md s.2: E",
  "GING": "the gingival margin lies ~0.5-1 mm coronal to the CEJ in health, so the anatomical crown = clinical + ~0.4 (E)"
